ORIGINAL WORK AND ATTRIBUTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project began from "LLM Council" by Andrej Karpathy:

    https://github.com/karpathy/llm-council

That project introduced the multi-model deliberation approach on which the
general council mode is based — parallel model responses, anonymised peer
review with self-vote exclusion, and synthesis by a chairman model. Credit
for that idea belongs to its author.

This acknowledgement is permanent and unconditional. It does not lapse because
the implementation was rewritten, and it is to be carried forward into every
further application built on this foundation, in any jurisdiction. The insight
came first; everything here followed from it.

The upstream project carries no licence file. Its author released it publicly
stating it was "provided here as is for other people's inspiration". Because
no licence could be relied upon, the implementation here has since been
rewritten: the transport layer, the storage layer, every prompt, the route
handlers of the general council and the launch script were each reimplemented
in this project's own words. In November 2026 the general council's
vocabulary followed: its functions, the keys an exchange is stored under, its
stream events and its answer labels were renamed, so that an exchange is now
its answers, its reviews and its ruling rather than three numbered stages.

What remains in common with the original is of four kinds, and they are not
alike:

    The idea and its shape. Several models answer, referee one another
    blind, and a chair settles it. That is the upstream author's, it is
    credited above, and nothing here claims it.

    A few names. The configuration variables COUNCIL_MODELS, CHAIRMAN_MODEL
    and DATA_DIR, which running deployments are configured with; the
    /api/conversations routes; ordinary field names such as id, title and
    messages; and, in the compliance panel's own event stream, names of the
    form stage1_complete. Conversations stored before the renaming are still
    read, so the old keys also survive in one translation table in
    backend/storage.py.

    Library and tool idiom. Import statements, the calls any user of
    FastAPI, httpx or fetch writes, and files a tool generated — the Vite
    React template and the uv project files.

    Blank lines, brackets, docstring delimiters and bare section headings.

Measured by `git blame` on 16 November 2026, 457 lines of the tracked text
files, lock files apart, are still byte-identical to upstream: 270 of the
fourth kind, 169 of the third and 18 of the second. None of them is a prompt,
a comment, a docstring or a sentence of documentation. The method and the
per-file figures are in docs/upstream-provenance.md, so the count can be run
again rather than taken on trust.

